# kernel-trim.config — shrink multi_v7 to fit boot.img before the factory-bad
# erase block at boot-relative 0x920000 (9.2 MiB). Disables big visual/audio/net
# subsystems not needed for headless NAND RW-ubifs bring-up. Multi_v7's proven
# boot core is kept; only bloat cut. Re-enable later (properly adapted to
# mainline) when aligning to vendor's display/ethernet fragments for project work.
#
# Merged AFTER multi_v7_defconfig + kernel.config so these override.
# CONFIG_DRM is not set
# CONFIG_MEDIA_SUPPORT is not set
# CONFIG_SOUND is not set
# CONFIG_USB_SUPPORT is not set
# CONFIG_WLAN is not set
# CONFIG_STAGING is not set
# CONFIG_NFC is not set
# CONFIG_INPUT_JOYSTICK is not set
# CONFIG_INPUT_TABLET is not set
# CONFIG_HID is not set
# --- big subsystems found via vmlinux .o sizing (each ~0.5-3 MiB) ---
# CONFIG_NETWORK_FILESYSTEMS is not set   # NFS/CIFS/sunrpc (~3 MiB)
# CONFIG_EXT4_FS is not set                # (~1.5 MiB)
# CONFIG_BTRFS_FS is not set
# CONFIG_F2FS_FS is not set
# CONFIG_XFS_FS is not set
# CONFIG_PERF_EVENTS is not set            # (~0.8 MiB)
# KEEP: NET core (ethernet later), ubifs, squashfs, proc/sysfs/tmpfs.
# Pin TMPFS explicitly: multi_v7 only sets TMPFS_POSIX_ACL, so TMPFS rides on
# its default y — but the merge_config + olddefconfig pass can drop it to n
# (observed on the board: .config had "# CONFIG_TMPFS is not set"). With TMPFS
# off, `mount -t tmpfs` falls back to ramfs, which rejects the mode= option
# buildroot's /etc/fstab uses → "/tmp unknown parameter 'mode'". Pin it so the
# KEEP comment above actually holds.
CONFIG_TMPFS=y
